.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAG-GET-ROUTE 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eag-get-route \- show one gateway route's definition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eag get-route
.BR \-\-route\-id | \-r
.I ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows one route's definition: the path it publishes, the application
behind it, what it requires of a caller, and whether it is currently in
service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-route\-id " " \fIID\fR
Route to show. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The route was found. Its definition is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing arguments, no administrator session, no such route, or the
server rejected the request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eag get-route --route-id datenlieferanten
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eag (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eag-list-routes (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eag-update-route (1)
